    "fact_rationales": {
      "F10": "Intraoperative frozen sections showing granulomatous inflammation support several candidates, including sarcoidosis, foreign body granuloma, granuloma annulare, necrobiotic xanthogranuloma, and rheumatoid nodule.",
      "F11": "Final histopathology showing granulomatous inflammation with central necrobiosis and extensive Alcian-Blue positive mucin is more characteristic of granuloma annulare and less typical of foreign body granuloma, necrobiotic xanthogranuloma, and rheumatoid nodule, but can be seen in sarcoidosis.",
      "F12": "The absence of malignancy does not differentially support any of the candidates, as none are primarily malignant conditions.",
      "F9": "CT scan finding of soft-tissue thickening without bony invasion is non-specific and does not strongly favor any candidate."
